# Host files

The edge where files and the environment come in. Every file the factory keeps —
trails, ledgers, artifacts, results — goes through these, and they work in a
test's sealed world (an in-memory filesystem), so the code that keeps state on
disk is tested without touching a disk.

## Note
A file's text, a file replaced, and text added to the end of a file (created when
absent) — how every ledger grows, so an entry once written is never rewritten.

## To readText (path: Text) -> Result of Text and Text:
    Return read(path).

## To writeText (path: Text, content: Text) -> Result of Unit and Text:
    Return write(path, content).

## To appendText (path: Text, content: Text) -> Result of Unit and Text:
    Return appendFile(path, content).

## Note
Whether anything is at a path, the sorted names in a directory, and a directory
made with every directory above it.

## To pathExists (path: Text) -> Bool:
    Return fileExists(path).

## To listNames (dir: Text) -> Result of Seq of Text and Text:
    Return listDir(dir).

## To ensureDir (dir: Text) -> Result of Unit and Text:
    Return makeDirs(dir).

## Note
A file replaced all at once: written beside itself, then renamed over the old,
so a reader sees the old content or the new and never half of either.

## To writeAtomically (path: Text, content: Text) -> Result of Unit and Text:
    Inspect write(path + ".tmp", content):
        When Err (e):
            Return a new Err with error e.
        When Ok (done):
            Return renameFile(path + ".tmp", path).
    Return a new Err with error "unwritten".

## Note
One line added to a file in a directory, the directory made first.

## To appendLine (dir: Text, name: Text, line: Text) -> Result of Unit and Text:
    Let made be makeDirs(dir).
    Return appendFile(dir + "/" + name, line + "\n").

## Note
An environment variable, or `fallback` when it is unset or blank; the program's
arguments (its own name first); and the time in Unix milliseconds.

## To envOr (name: Text, fallback: Text) -> Text:
    Inspect get(name):
        When Some (v):
            If trim(v) is equal to "":
                Return fallback.
            Return v.
        When None:
            Return fallback.
    Return fallback.

## To programArgs () -> Seq of Text:
    Return args().

## To clockMs () -> Int:
    Return now().

## Test: an atomic write replaces a file whole and leaves no temporary behind

Let first be writeAtomically("ledger.json", "first").
Let second be writeAtomically("ledger.json", "second").
Expect that readText("ledger.json") is equal to a new Ok with value "second".
Expect that pathExists("ledger.json.tmp") is equal to false.

## Test: lines are appended one at a time under a made directory

Let a be appendLine("trails/opdp", "116.jsonl", "one").
Let b be appendLine("trails/opdp", "116.jsonl", "two").
Expect that readText("trails/opdp/116.jsonl") is equal to a new Ok with value "one\ntwo\n".
Expect that listNames("trails/opdp") is equal to a new Ok with value ["116.jsonl"].

## Test: a sealed world has no environment to read

Expect that envOr("MACSAD_LARGO", "largo") is equal to "largo".

## Test: a file exists exactly when it was written

For all booleans written:
    If written:
        Let w be writeText("maybe.txt", "x").
    Expect that pathExists("maybe.txt") is equal to written.
